WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:01.880
Wren: It's discouraging.

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.680
Carmichael:

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:05.200
W: [clearing throat]

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:06.760
W:

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:10.040
W: So, now that we have all the cameras together, we can sync them up, but...

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:11.080
W: ...how do we do that?

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.280
W: I'm gonna start rolling.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.640
W: And they are rolling now.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.080
W: Sync it with my helmet.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:18.300
W: [anticipatory breath]

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.220
SFX: Woody thunk, slice, splatter

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:21.720
SFX: Portal shot

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.000
W: I connected all of them to this remote here.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.840
W: Somehow, for syncing it, you can do, like, a visual, like -

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:27.520
W: ...a clapperboard sorta style, but...

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.000
W: I don't know how you're supposed to clap for something that's looking everywhere.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.160
W: So, my solution is, literally, to take this helmet,

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.280
W: ...drape it over,

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.640
W: ...hold it for, like, a couple seconds,

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:36.460
W: ...then take it out.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:37.120
SFX: Portal shot

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.680
W: Like, eight feet. I'm gonna say this is - this is, like, ten feet away.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.320
W: Here we are at twenty feet away.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.440
W: Actually probably closer to, like, thirty feet.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.880
W: If we're out in a public spot, I wouldn't really wanna go any further than this.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:49.580
W: Huh.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:51.820
W: Oh my god.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:53.980
C:

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.100
W [discouraged]: Not good.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:58.980
W: Hardcore bad... -ly stitched together.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:01.500
W: Today is Monday. We're shooting the main video on Thursday,
Music: Vanishing Point, Corridor Digital

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:05.740
W: ...and this is not a promising test. I've got, basically, two days to figure this out.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.500
W: We have to have a good solution by the end of Wednesday.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.020
W: And right now...

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:18.620
W: ...it sucks.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:20.460
SFX: Rising drumroll

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.740
Allen: Here, d'you wanna hold this? [laughing]

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:25.380
A: Luke Skywalker's lightsaber from A New Hope.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.540
Brandon: So, Allen made this. This is a real-life lightsaber.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.780
SFX: Lightsaber startup

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.100
A: Okay, so, you turn on the coil,

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.420
B: Yeah?
Sam: [indistinct]

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.580
A: So, I push down, nothing happens, that's fine.
SFX: Lihtsaber stratup

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:38.020
B: Yeah?
A: Turn the fuel off, grows hotter -

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:38.520
SFX: Lightsaber startup

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:39.360
SFX: Choir swelling

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.600
SFX: Choir swelling, slowed lightsaber startup

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.040
B:

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.180
A: [laughing]

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:45.420
D: So, what's your safe word?

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:47.760
S: [cry of fake-pain]

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:49.600
A, B, D, N: [laughing]

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:50.960
D: Towards the camera.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:52.360
S: [cry of fake-pain]

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:53.220
A, D, N: [laughing]

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:54.160
B: [victory cry]
A, D, N: [laughing]

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:58.640
S: [cry of fake-pain]
A, D, N: [laughing, cheering]

00:01:59.060 --> 00:01:59.560
B: Okay!
S: [cry of fake-pain]

